Fluent GTK theme
----------------

CachyOS-Nord is a modified version of the Fluent GTK theme by vinceliuice
(https://github.com/vinceliuice/Fluent-gtk-theme), licensed under GPL-3.0.
Modified in October 2026:

- recolored throughout to the CachyOS Nord color scheme (below), keeping only
  the dark color variant, with Fluent's branding removed
- widget styling from the cachyOS-nord theme: outlined checks and radios, the
  rectangular switch, joined stack switchers, filled list selections and the cyan
  window glow
- larger title buttons that glow on hover, and matching header bar heights in
  GTK 3 and GTK 4
- the Budgie panel, popovers and Raven sharing the title bar color
- a librsvg renderer (src/render-svg-ids.py) used by the asset scripts when
  Inkscape is not installed
- themes for Alacritty, Ghostty and btop in the same colors (src/apps)

The Firefox theme in src/firefox keeps its own credits (see src/firefox/README.md).


CachyOS color scheme and widget styling
---------------------------------------

The color scheme comes from the cachyOS-nord GTK theme in CachyOS-Nord-KDE by
CachyOS (https://github.com/CachyOS/CachyOS-Nord-KDE):

- navy backgrounds #0F121C, #131621 and #181B28
- the cyan accent and text color #47ADD6, and #147AA3 for links
- the status colors #7AE070 (success), #ADAD70 (warning) and #AD7AA3 (error)
- the dark cyan shadows #0A242F and #15485D
- for the terminal themes in src/apps: red #BF616A, blue #81A1C1 and white #D8DEE9,
  from CachyOS's Nordic Konsole scheme
  (konsole/cachyOSNord.colorscheme in the same repository)

So does the styling listed above as coming from the cachyOS-nord theme. The
check, dash and dot glyphs in src/gtk/scalable/classic-*-symbolic.svg are taken
from that theme's assets; that theme was itself generated with Oomox, a fork of
the Numix GTK theme.

The CachyOS-Nord-KDE repository does not include a license file. CachyOS
distributes it as the package cachyos-nord-gtk-theme-git, licensed GPL3
(https://dashboard.cachyos.org/package/cachyos/any/cachyos-nord-gtk-theme-git,
checked on 2026-10-30). The material above is used under that license.
